3. Rules that apply to all three loads
#
Rule
R1
Reload pattern: clear the table with DELETE (not TRUNCATE), then insert. Running the load twice must give the same result.
R2
Read the date offset from dw.EtlConfig. Never hard-code it in the query.
R3
Apply the offset to source dates before looking up DimDate. Convert datetime values to DATE first, so time-of-day cannot break the match.
R4
Surrogate keys, not natural keys. Facts store the dimension's ...Key, found by joining on the dimension's natural ...ID column.
R5
Unknown member: when a lookup finds no match, store -1 instead of NULL or dropping the row. Use COALESCE.
R6
Order date is mandatory. If an order date finds no calendar row, the row must not be silently kept with a wrong key. The row-count check (section 6) exists to catch this.
R7
No row multiplication. Every join must return at most one row per source row. If your row count is higher than the source, a join is fanning out.
R8
Match the target column types shown in each table below. Money measures keep their precision.
R9
Write an explicit column list in the INSERT, not positional columns.
